'' T21, RUN: an out-of-range WRITE to a REDIM-ed array under -exx stops with runtime error
'' 6 and exit 6, fbc's message word for word. Before T21 the write went past the block and
'' the program exited 0. Nothing is printed first: the abort goes to stderr unbuffered
'' and a print would race it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/boundchk-dyn-run.bas -o tests/codegen/boundchkdynrun.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/boundchkdynrun.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/boundchkdynrun.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: runtime error 6 (out of bounds array access) at line 4 of
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 'A' accessed with invalid index = 9, must be between 1 and 3
